 "traps": [
  "the modules do not inherit from the root pom.xml, a pure aggregator; each imports the Quarkus BOM itself, and rest-narration also imports the LangChain4j BOM",
  "Quarkus extensions bring the frameworks: quarkus-rest-jackson gives Quarkus REST and Jackson, quarkus-hibernate-orm-panache gives Hibernate ORM and Panache, quarkus-messaging-kafka gives SmallRye Reactive Messaging, quarkus-apicurio-registry-avro gives Apache Avro",
  "each module has its own frameworks: only grpc-locations has Protocol Buffers and MockK, only rest-narration has LangChain4j, only rest-fights uses MongoDB with Panache",
  "the React front end in ui-super-heroes/src/main/webui is an npm unit of its own, built through Quinoa by the Maven module; Jest runs only through react-scripts test",
  "health, metrics, OpenTelemetry, Kubernetes, Helm, OpenShift, container-image, Stork, Fault Tolerance, Liquibase, validation and OpenAPI extensions are not counted as frameworks here",
  "the services are started by compose files spread over module folders (src/main/docker-compose/infra.yml, deploy/docker-compose/*.yml, monitoring/); MariaDB serves grpc-locations, PostgreSQL rest-heroes and rest-villains",
  "OpenAI is reached only through LangChain4j configuration (quarkus.langchain4j.openai.api-key); in dev and test WireMock stands in for it, and Microcks is a dev service, not a service of the product",
  "only frameworks and services are measured; the other facets are in unknown"
 ],
 "cases": [
  "framework-through-plugin",
  "framework-per-unit",
  "test-only-framework",
